# Coding Convention and Maintainability Rule

## Core standards
- Follow language/framework idioms and project style guides.
- Use explicit naming and cohesive module boundaries.
- Avoid dead code, duplicate logic, and hidden side effects.
- Keep functions focused and testable.

## Safety standards
- No silent exception swallowing.
- No TODO/FIXME left in production-critical paths without tracker reference.
- No unsafe type usage in typed codebases when strict alternatives exist.

## Review gate
- Changes must include rationale ("why"), not only mechanical edits.
- Any risky refactor must include regression test coverage.
- No DONE claim without reproducible build/test evidence.
